  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $A, B$ are two events such that $P(A \\cup B) \\geq \\frac{3}{4}$ and $\\frac{1}{8} \\leq P(A \\cap B) \\leq \\frac{3}{8},$ then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uUYp1",
      "text": "$P(A)+P(B) \\leq \\frac{11}{8}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jeQuT",
      "text": "$P(A) \\cdot P(B) \\leq \\frac{3}{8}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hniIm",
      "text": "$P(A)+P(B) \\geq \\frac{7}{8}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4pNB1",
      "text": "None of the above",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know,\r\n$$\r\nP(A \\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A \\cap B)\r\n$$\r\n$\\Rightarrow P(A)+P(B)=P(A \\cup B)+P(A \\cap B)$\r\nGiven, $\\quad \\frac{3}{4} \\leq P(A \\cup B) \\leq 1$\r\nand $\\quad \\frac{1}{8} \\leq P(A \\cap B) \\leq \\frac{3}{8}$\r\nSo. $\\quad \\frac{7}{8} \\leq P(A \\cup B)+P(A \\cap B) \\leq \\frac{11}{8}$\r\n$\\therefore P(A)+P(B) \\geq \\frac{7}{8}$ and $P(A)+P(B) \\leq \\frac{11}{8}$",
    "image": null
  },
